5,1,1,talk,Kenji,,The depot floor never stops. I need to know if the new system can handle our actual yard chaos.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,I am worried about the hidden costs that appear after the initial approval. The headline price is a trap.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I need to know who is actually accountable when the system fails. Ambiguity in ownership is a critical risk we cannot afford.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Rin,,"I keep seeing old tools that nobody updates, and then we pay extra to fix the mess. I want to check the upgrade history.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Servas,,"I worry about the people who hold this system together. If we change it, who is left to carry the weight?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, that upgrade history is key. If the dispatch tool is stuck, the yard will grind to a halt.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, accountability is vital, but I need to see the renewal invoices. The real cost often hides in those recurring fees.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I agree. But I need to see the support ownership records from the last outage. That shows who actually stepped up when things broke.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, exactly! If the tool is stuck, everything jams. I will check the upgrade history to see if they actually fix things or just patch them.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
