35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The yard hardware is a mess, and the 2021 trial failed fast. Plus, we have no freeze window in winter.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, the board minutes show capital gets cut, but operating lines pass easily. That is where the real money leaks.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, that aligns with my findings. Support was unowned for two days last winter. The scope also shifted twice. We are walking into the same trap.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, the dispatch tool skipped three upgrades! It just aged in place. And the supervisors ignored the new steps. We need a vendor who actually fixes things, not just patches them!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, the supervisors dropping the steps confirms my fear. We are losing two admins, and the last hire took eleven months. Who will teach the new system?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, that skipped upgrade history is terrifying. If the yard hardware is already mixed, a new system might not even talk to our scanners.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, hardware mismatch is a capital risk, but the invoices show add-ons climbing yearly. That recurring bleed is what I fear most.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, the skipped upgrades confirm the pattern. If the vendor cannot maintain the system, the initial plan is irrelevant. I need to see who owns the fix.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, exactly! If they can’t fix it, the plan is useless. I need a vendor who stays to repair the mess, not just install it and vanish!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, ownership is vital, but without the people to hold it, the system fails. We must protect the remaining admins from being stretched thin.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, the hiring gap is brutal. If we lose the admins, the yard devices become useless bricks. We need a vendor who trains the floor crew, not just the office.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Servas, the people are critical, but the invoices prove the trap. Bundled deals stay flat, while add-ons climb. We must lock the total cost now.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, the invoices show the bleed, but my data shows the structural failure. We need a single point of accountability, not just a lower price.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, I agree! But if the vendor leaves, the add-ons are useless. I need a partner who stays to fix the aging mess, not just sell us more!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Mizuki, the cost is real, but the human cost is higher. If we cannot retain the knowledge, the savings are an illusion.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, locking costs is smart, but I need the system to survive the November rush. A cheap tool that crashes in winter is worthless to the yard.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, a crash in winter is a capital disaster. I will ensure the contract locks the total life cost so we are not blindsided by hidden fees later.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, a crash is a symptom. The root cause is the lack of a single owner. I need a vendor who answers for the whole system, not just the parts.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, if it crashes, who fixes it? I need a vendor who stays to repair the aging mess, not just install it and vanish!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the yard must keep moving. But a system that ignores the people who run it will fail. We need a vendor who respects the human rhythm.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
